investigators in Brazil are trying to  determine what caused a massive fire  that engulfed a 200 year old National  Museum in Rio de Janeiro last night more  than 20 million historical artifacts  were destroyed some 80 firefighters were  called in to battle the brave the blaze  and president Michel temer called it a  sad day for all Brazilians anne-marie  green is following this ann-marie good  morning good morning well firefighters  got a slow start to putting out the  flames because two of the fire hydrants  closest to the building were not working  the fire started Sunday evening after  visiting hours so it was closed to the  public at the time firefighters and  several museum workers would race to  save the museum's relics it took more  than three hours to put out the flames  the museum had a vast collection of  artifacts donated by the Brazilian royal  family the national treasure house  artifacts from Egypt greco-roman art and  the first human remains found in Brazil  dating back almost 12,000 years the  museum was connected to University so  some of the pieces were spared from the  fire it's not immediately clear just how  the fire began though and there are no  reports of injuries  yeah all right Anna Marie thank you
 

